nd W9 same. \n\nBut considering that I have a Chi of T3-T4-T5, maybe keeping T9 is not part of that. So discarding T9 is safe. \n\nSo I'll go with Play T9.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The current hand lacks a pair, so the priority is to discard a tile that doesn't block potential sequences or pairs. Keeping B2-B3-B4 as a chow is critical. Discarding T9 (a terminal) is safe as it\u2019s not part of any sequence and has no immediate use in melds.  \nReason: T9 is a terminal tile with no connection to existing melds or potential sequences. Discarding it preserves flexibility for forming pairs or chows with remaining tiles like B2-B3-B4 or T4.  \nAnswer: Play T9"}
